<title>MEXICO: Mexico's April coffee exports fall from April '96.</title>
<headline>Mexico's April coffee exports fall from April '96.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican coffee exports totalled 451,590 60-kg bags for April, a fall from the 528,944 bags exported in the same month in the previous year, the Mexican Coffee Council said in a report obtained by Reuters Thursday.</p>
<p>Growers said the fall in exports could be attributed to some farmers waiting to sell to prolong a season of high coffee prices through May.  </p>
<p>The coffee figures for April are preliminary, the council said. It also revised some past export numbers.</p>
<p>Mexico's exports for the first seven months of the 1996-1997 cycle totalled 3,706,735 bags compared with 3,468,567 bags during the same period in the 1995-1996 crop.</p>
<p>A full breakdown of the Mexican exports follows in table form. Figures are for 60-kg bags.  </p>
<p>    Month     1996-1997	 1995-1996	    1994-1995</p>
<p>    October     163,489	   101,912		 59,303</p>
<p>    November    320,842	   296,810		131,767</p>
<p>    December    390,111	   421,445		260,081</p>
<p>    January     871,321	   745,428		586,669</p>
<p>    February    837,812	   744,586		460,060</p>
<p>    March	 671,570	   633,648		603,537</p>
<p>    April	 451,590	   528,944		243,772</p>
<p>    May				 456,768		287,238</p>
<p>    June				193,627		217,951</p>
<p>    July				219,432		121,033</p>
<p>    August			    146,745		184,466</p>
<p>    September			  86,982		101,867</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
